WEBVTT

00:00:09.940 --> 00:00:15.750
Full energy is troubled because there's no place to go

00:00:16.210 --> 00:00:22.030
A slight shake destroys boredom

00:00:22.320 --> 00:00:28.170
I Ride, On the White Line  OH, OH, OH

00:00:28.420 --> 00:00:34.240
Sit Down  At the place I trust  OH, OH, OH

00:00:34.430 --> 00:00:37.540
We can go even if we're lost

00:00:37.770 --> 00:00:43.650
Everyone receives freedom and passion

00:00:44.040 --> 00:00:49.850
We were born to shine, and our journey continues

00:00:50.180 --> 00:00:56.060
Your soul is the key that supports our uncertain days

00:00:56.350 --> 00:01:02.000
The best growth creates an unstoppable WILD DRIVE

00:01:02.420 --> 00:01:08.270
We still quietly knock on the door

00:01:18.860 --> 00:01:21.560
I knew something bad would happen.

00:01:21.560 --> 00:01:25.230
Shizuka was dragged into a duel.

00:01:25.440 --> 00:01:29.520
Even though it's 3-on-1, Honda and Shizuka are amateurs.

00:01:30.060 --> 00:01:34.620
The Big Five take advantage by focusing their attack on Shizuka.

00:01:34.620 --> 00:01:38.460
No!  Honda lost his life points to protect Shizuka!

00:01:38.760 --> 00:01:42.500
Honda, I won't let your sacrifice go to waste!

00:01:43.020 --> 00:01:49.020
St. Joan
The Trinity's Attack

00:01:53.800 --> 00:01:55.660
What was that scream?

00:01:55.660 --> 00:01:59.180
I have a bad feeling.

00:01:59.530 --> 00:02:00.640
Let's hurry!

00:02:00.640 --> 00:02:01.980
Jonouchi!

00:02:02.200 --> 00:02:05.040
Hey!  Wait up!

00:02:11.770 --> 00:02:13.000
Honda...

00:02:13.550 --> 00:02:14.880
Honda...

00:02:15.980 --> 00:02:18.480
Honda sacrificed himself for me.

00:02:23.600 --> 00:02:24.850
Shizuka...

00:02:25.170 --> 00:02:26.450
Young lady.

00:02:29.110 --> 00:02:30.970
It's your turn.

00:02:36.940 --> 00:02:38.200
Stand up, Shizuka!

00:02:39.240 --> 00:02:40.700
What are you doing?

00:02:41.900 --> 00:02:43.370
Hurry up.

00:02:45.260 --> 00:02:47.240
Stand up, Shizuka!

00:02:47.240 --> 00:02:49.340
So you're ending your turn?

00:02:53.280 --> 00:02:57.370
Shizuka can't even think about this duel.

00:02:57.370 --> 00:02:58.730
I must do something.

00:03:01.260 --> 00:03:03.920
It's my fault that Honda is...

00:03:04.200 --> 00:03:06.100
What should I do now?

00:03:06.610 --> 00:03:10.530
Shizuka!  Stand up and fight by my side!

00:03:10.860 --> 00:03:12.510
The duel isn't over!

00:03:12.510 --> 00:03:15.970
Honda may return if we win!

00:03:17.410 --> 00:03:18.820
Shizuka...

00:03:20.650 --> 00:03:21.850
My turn!

00:03:23.910 --> 00:03:24.990
I draw!

00:03:27.680 --> 00:03:33.360
I'll do whatever I can and eliminate as many life points as possible.

00:03:33.560 --> 00:03:36.180
I activate Dimensionhole from my hand!

00:03:36.740 --> 00:03:41.170
Dimensionhole withdraws Dark Assailant!

00:03:45.140 --> 00:03:51.220
Since Dark Assailant is gone, Machine King loses 100 attack points.

00:03:51.770 --> 00:03:53.480
Big deal.

00:03:53.740 --> 00:03:56.700
I'm only getting started.  I play a spell card.

00:03:56.700 --> 00:04:01.080
A spell card won't topple Machine King.

00:04:01.300 --> 00:04:02.760
Even this one?

00:04:04.460 --> 00:04:06.560
What?  Dice Dungeon?

00:04:06.560 --> 00:04:13.800
When Dimension Dice and Dice Dungeon are both on the field, they create a Dungeon Dice Field.

00:04:15.200 --> 00:04:17.370
So that set card is...

00:04:17.580 --> 00:04:19.080
Exactly.

00:04:19.600 --> 00:04:21.480
Dimension Dice!

00:04:22.420 --> 00:04:23.940
What?

00:04:24.160 --> 00:04:28.880
Ryuji Otogi, you're the creator of Dungeon Dice Monsters.

00:04:28.880 --> 00:04:31.880
I was surprised when I found this card.

00:04:31.880 --> 00:04:34.550
I never imagined you'd have DDM cards.

00:04:34.760 --> 00:04:36.040
I see.

00:04:36.040 --> 00:04:39.170
When Pegasus was using your game data...

00:04:39.170 --> 00:04:46.230
...it must've transferred from Industrial Illusions to Kaiba Corporation's computers.

00:04:46.600 --> 00:04:49.900
I tribute The 13th Grave and Yaranzo.

00:04:50.180 --> 00:04:52.260
I summon Orgoth the Relentless!

00:05:01.960 --> 00:05:11.020
By tributing two Machine-Type monsters, Machine King loses 200 attack points.

00:05:13.470 --> 00:05:18.960
We both choose one monster on our fields and place them in the Dungeon Area.

00:05:18.960 --> 00:05:24.100
We roll dice and take the corresponding number's effect.  Then we battle.

00:05:24.320 --> 00:05:26.680
Fine.  I choose Machine King.

00:05:27.630 --> 00:05:30.360
I choose Orgoth the Relentless.

00:05:31.600 --> 00:05:33.480
Here I go!  Dice roll!

00:05:41.910 --> 00:05:45.370
By rolling a 6, the field doubles my attack points.

00:05:45.370 --> 00:05:49.660
Good.  Orgoth the Relentless's attack points are doubled!

00:05:52.400 --> 00:05:55.410
So it all depends on the roll.

00:06:02.280 --> 00:06:05.960
By rolling a 1, the field takes away 1000 attack points.

00:06:06.300 --> 00:06:07.160
Damn.

00:06:09.320 --> 00:06:11.630
Let's go, Orgoth the Relentless!

00:06:16.900 --> 00:06:18.550
Attack Machine King!

00:06:23.040 --> 00:06:24.980
Diamond Blade!

00:06:29.330 --> 00:06:31.020
Machine King is destroyed!

00:06:31.020 --> 00:06:32.140
I end my turn!

00:06:32.360 --> 00:06:33.170
You punk.

00:06:33.170 --> 00:06:35.140
My turn.  I draw.

00:06:37.740 --> 00:06:43.510
I summon myself - the Deck Master Robotic Knight - in attack position.

00:06:47.100 --> 00:06:51.620
I activate Recycling Plant from my hand.

00:06:51.840 --> 00:06:58.560
This card revives a Machine-Type monster from my graveyard and fuses with me.

00:06:58.780 --> 00:07:00.500
Be my strength!

00:07:00.500 --> 00:07:02.920
Revive, Machine King!

00:07:14.120 --> 00:07:15.150
What?

00:07:18.680 --> 00:07:26.990
Perfect Machine King gains 500 attack points for every Machine-Type monster on the field.

00:07:27.320 --> 00:07:30.930
Since there are three, that's 1500 points!

00:07:31.140 --> 00:07:34.770
Wrong.  I'm Machine-Type too.

00:07:34.770 --> 00:07:37.050
I gain 2000 attack points.

00:07:39.100 --> 00:07:45.000
And Clockwork Night gives me 500 attack points!

00:07:46.570 --> 00:07:48.700
Damn!  Unbelievable!

00:07:54.780 --> 00:08:00.720
Due to your Field Spell's effect, we'll battle in the Dice Dungeon.

00:08:01.170 --> 00:08:02.870
It'll all depend on the roll.

00:08:03.420 --> 00:08:05.660
I choose Orgoth the Relentless!

00:08:06.370 --> 00:08:07.110
Here I go.

00:08:14.060 --> 00:08:17.370
By rolling a 5, my attack points are halved.

00:08:18.350 --> 00:08:21.910
My original attack points may be halved...

00:08:21.910 --> 00:08:29.390
...but due to my Machine-Type effects and Clockwork Night, I still have 3850 attack points.

00:08:30.740 --> 00:08:33.760
Orgoth the Relentless has 2500 attack points.

00:08:33.760 --> 00:08:36.540
I can't win unless I make a good roll.

00:08:37.080 --> 00:08:39.500
I won't waste Honda's sacrifice!

00:08:39.500 --> 00:08:40.360
Dice roll!

00:08:45.070 --> 00:08:47.900
By rolling a 1, I lose 1000 attack points.

00:08:49.300 --> 00:08:50.740
It's over.

00:08:51.000 --> 00:08:53.280
Perish, Orgoth the Relentless!

00:08:58.610 --> 00:09:02.080
The remaining attack points strike you!

00:09:06.250 --> 00:09:10.110
At this rate, Otogi will lose too.

00:09:10.480 --> 00:09:14.900
I can't do anything.  But...

00:09:19.080 --> 00:09:23.210
Since Orgoth the Relentless is destroyed, Dice Dungeon is also destroyed.

00:09:23.660 --> 00:09:27.510
Damn.  Even Orgoth the Relentless couldn't win.

00:09:27.510 --> 00:09:31.950
If Honda was here, us three could've worked together.

00:09:35.050 --> 00:09:37.140
You're on the brink of defeat.

00:09:37.140 --> 00:09:38.820
I end my turn.

00:09:38.820 --> 00:09:43.310
He's having trouble against amateurs.

00:09:43.310 --> 00:09:48.040
I hope he can defeat them completely.

00:09:50.220 --> 00:09:56.450
Even though you invented Dungeon Dice Monsters, you're an amateur duelist.

00:09:56.850 --> 00:10:00.880
I usually don't duel against amateurs.

00:10:01.400 --> 00:10:05.970
I must get my revenge against him!

00:10:17.170 --> 00:10:20.030
As you ordered, I destroyed Alcatraz.

00:10:20.400 --> 00:10:22.200
Good.  Confirmed.

00:10:22.660 --> 00:10:26.630
Starting today, Kaiba Corporation's military department is dissolved.

00:10:26.960 --> 00:10:30.070
Proceed with the Duel Tower Project instead.

00:10:30.280 --> 00:10:31.480
And me?

00:10:31.480 --> 00:10:36.080
You can procure supplies for the Duel Tower.

00:10:36.730 --> 00:10:40.500
Follow your supervisor's orders and don't get in anyone's way.

00:10:40.500 --> 00:10:41.530
That's all.

00:10:45.450 --> 00:10:46.860
Seto Kaiba.

00:10:46.860 --> 00:10:49.320
You humiliated me.

00:10:49.880 --> 00:10:52.540
But the kid gave me another chance.

00:10:52.540 --> 00:10:55.260
Once I defeat these two, you're next!

00:10:55.640 --> 00:10:57.860
Shizuka, it's your turn.

00:10:58.260 --> 00:11:01.910
Shape up!  Don't let Honda's sacrifice go to waste!

00:11:03.610 --> 00:11:07.300
Otogi may lose because of me.

00:11:07.880 --> 00:11:11.840
Hurry up!  Or can you no longer fight?

00:11:11.840 --> 00:11:13.780
I have to do something.

00:11:13.780 --> 00:11:16.740
But what can I do?

00:11:16.740 --> 00:11:19.490
What should I do, brother?

00:11:33.120 --> 00:11:34.660
Get up, Shizuka!

00:11:34.660 --> 00:11:36.370
If you give up, it's over!

00:11:36.660 --> 00:11:38.810
Stand and fight to the end!

00:11:39.860 --> 00:11:46.660
This may be your final chance to attack, but I guess you're ending your turn.

00:11:46.880 --> 00:11:50.040
She's not ending her turn!  Shizuka!

00:11:50.040 --> 00:11:52.850
Remember!  No specific instructions!

00:11:59.400 --> 00:12:01.530
Shizuka, try to remember.

00:12:02.160 --> 00:12:05.020
You watched Jonouchi's duel.

00:12:05.360 --> 00:12:08.700
Jonouchi never gave up.

00:12:09.100 --> 00:12:11.960
My brother's duel?

00:12:12.370 --> 00:12:15.460
It's my turn!  Serket attacks!

00:12:15.460 --> 00:12:18.480
The next victim is Insect Queen!

00:12:22.030 --> 00:12:24.340
Brother...  No...

00:12:24.340 --> 00:12:26.500
I can't watch!

00:12:26.860 --> 00:12:28.430
Don't run away, Shizuka!

00:12:28.430 --> 00:12:29.800
Keep watching me!

00:12:30.620 --> 00:12:33.660
I might lose.

00:12:33.900 --> 00:12:36.600
But I want you to watch me to the end.

00:12:37.040 --> 00:12:39.400
He never gave up.

00:12:39.400 --> 00:12:42.670
My brother dueled confidently to the end.

00:12:43.360 --> 00:12:46.540
Brother, I'll fight to the end!

00:12:46.980 --> 00:12:47.980
Shizuka!

00:12:50.060 --> 00:12:51.120
Shizuka...

00:12:51.770 --> 00:12:55.710
Yugi, does Jonouchi knows the way?

00:12:55.710 --> 00:12:56.730
I don't know.

00:12:56.730 --> 00:12:59.420
But we have to trust Jonouchi!

00:13:01.430 --> 00:13:03.360
Over there!  I'm sure of it!

00:13:08.900 --> 00:13:11.720
Shizuka!

00:13:15.660 --> 00:13:16.740
Brother!

00:13:17.040 --> 00:13:18.170
Shizuka.

00:13:20.100 --> 00:13:21.940
Yugi!  Anzu!

00:13:22.160 --> 00:13:23.160
Otogi!

00:13:23.160 --> 00:13:24.950
We're back together!

00:13:24.950 --> 00:13:27.030
You finally arrived.

00:13:27.860 --> 00:13:29.060
Good timing.

00:13:29.060 --> 00:13:32.650
Watch your friends fall.

00:13:32.860 --> 00:13:34.280
The Big Five!

00:13:34.280 --> 00:13:37.420
Shizuka!  What are you doing there?

00:13:37.420 --> 00:13:38.960
Where's Honda?

00:13:38.960 --> 00:13:40.260
Weren't you together?

00:13:41.940 --> 00:13:43.800
Yeah.  But...

00:13:43.800 --> 00:13:45.930
He defeated him.

00:13:45.930 --> 00:13:46.820
No way!

00:13:47.130 --> 00:13:48.260
Oh no!

00:13:48.570 --> 00:13:49.770
Honda?

00:13:49.770 --> 00:13:51.870
You're lying.

00:13:52.080 --> 00:13:53.360
Why?

00:13:54.160 --> 00:13:55.770
It's not true!

00:13:55.770 --> 00:13:59.550
There's no way he'd lose!

00:13:59.900 --> 00:14:03.470
Brother...  I'm sorry.

00:14:03.470 --> 00:14:06.560
Honda lost to protect me.

00:14:07.240 --> 00:14:08.400
Shizuka...

00:14:08.400 --> 00:14:12.730
Jonouchi, the duel isn't over yet.

00:14:12.730 --> 00:14:15.130
If we win, Honda may return.

00:14:15.130 --> 00:14:16.660
You're right.

00:14:16.660 --> 00:14:18.670
Shizuka!  Switch places with me!

00:14:18.880 --> 00:14:20.270
That's not allowed.

00:14:20.270 --> 00:14:21.840
You'll be disqualified.

00:14:21.840 --> 00:14:23.400
Damn.

00:14:23.400 --> 00:14:25.650
Shizuka, listen carefully.

00:14:26.210 --> 00:14:30.740
Whatever the reason, you're a duelist if you're standing there.

00:14:32.000 --> 00:14:36.080
If you're my sister, don't give up until the end.

00:14:36.300 --> 00:14:40.120
Your brother will be watching.

00:14:40.860 --> 00:14:42.200
Brother...

00:14:43.780 --> 00:14:45.040
Shizuka.

00:14:45.700 --> 00:14:47.660
Watch me, brother.

00:14:52.530 --> 00:14:55.160
It's my turn.  I draw.

00:15:03.660 --> 00:15:08.460
Shizuka, stay calm and do what Honda taught you.

00:15:08.460 --> 00:15:09.330
Okay!

00:15:09.600 --> 00:15:12.330
What Honda taught me...

00:15:15.980 --> 00:15:21.360
Honda, please teach me about dueling before we arrive at Domino City.

00:15:21.360 --> 00:15:22.700
Sure.

00:15:23.200 --> 00:15:24.740
Let me think...

00:15:24.980 --> 00:15:30.800
I'm sure you know that when monsters battle, the one with higher attack points wins.

00:15:30.800 --> 00:15:34.640
But many strong monsters can't be played right away.

00:15:35.250 --> 00:15:39.110
Monster cards have star icons.

00:15:39.110 --> 00:15:43.880
If you want to summon powerful monsters with five or more stars...

00:15:43.880 --> 00:15:48.880
...you have to tribute one or two other monsters.

00:15:48.880 --> 00:15:51.260
Cards have stars?

00:15:51.260 --> 00:15:53.790
That's cute!  Like a ladybug!

00:15:54.950 --> 00:15:56.800
Ladybug...

00:15:56.800 --> 00:16:03.300
There's also a way of summoning powerful monsters by fusing multiple cards together.

00:16:03.300 --> 00:16:06.160
But you'll need a card called Polymerization.

00:16:06.160 --> 00:16:08.760
So tributing and Polymerization are key.

00:16:08.760 --> 00:16:10.100
That's right.

00:16:10.100 --> 00:16:12.220
I understand.

00:16:14.000 --> 00:16:15.210
Honda...

00:16:18.140 --> 00:16:22.090
Five stars...  That means I need to tribute to play this card.

00:16:25.800 --> 00:16:29.730
I feel bad, but Lady Panther has been turned into a machine.

00:16:29.940 --> 00:16:30.960
I'll use her.

00:16:31.180 --> 00:16:35.800
I tribute Lady Panther to summon Darklord Marie.

00:16:39.160 --> 00:16:40.230
Good.

00:16:41.230 --> 00:16:46.560
If we don't win this turn, we have no chance of defeating him.

00:16:46.560 --> 00:16:48.780
Go for it, Shizuka.

00:16:49.000 --> 00:16:50.960
Next is fusion.

00:16:50.960 --> 00:16:53.280
Which cards can I fuse?

00:16:53.280 --> 00:16:55.680
But I don't have Polymerization.

00:16:56.630 --> 00:16:57.720
Goddess?

00:16:57.960 --> 00:16:59.720
Leave it to me.

00:16:59.720 --> 00:17:03.830
Instead of Polymerization, you can discard a spell card...

00:17:03.830 --> 00:17:07.900
...to activate my Deck Master ability, Fusionic Eye.

00:17:08.240 --> 00:17:12.760
You can fuse monsters without Polymerization.

00:17:15.180 --> 00:17:17.380
Here's a spell card!

00:17:20.980 --> 00:17:25.240
I activate my Deck Master's ability, Fusionic Eye!

00:17:25.240 --> 00:17:31.520
I discard Magic Reflector to fuse Darklord Marie and The Forgiving Maiden.

00:17:32.600 --> 00:17:34.090
Fusionic Eye!

00:17:45.420 --> 00:17:48.680
So that's your strongest warrior.

00:17:49.080 --> 00:17:52.840
But she's no match for Perfect Machine King.

00:17:53.450 --> 00:17:54.180
What?

00:18:00.720 --> 00:18:01.950
You did it!

00:18:01.950 --> 00:18:08.930
Since St. Joan is Fairy-Type, Command Angel's effect raises her attack points by 400.

00:18:09.140 --> 00:18:12.360
Honda left Command Angel behind.

00:18:12.580 --> 00:18:15.820
St. Joan has 3200 attack points.

00:18:15.820 --> 00:18:21.580
His Deck Master, Perfect Machine King, has 4200 attack points.

00:18:21.800 --> 00:18:23.600
She's not strong enough.

00:18:24.370 --> 00:18:25.240
That's...

00:18:25.460 --> 00:18:27.580
Shizuka!  Otogi!

00:18:27.580 --> 00:18:29.660
The match is still up for grabs!

00:18:29.660 --> 00:18:31.680
You three have to work together!

00:18:32.120 --> 00:18:33.120
Three?

00:18:33.360 --> 00:18:37.560
Three?  But Honda is...

00:18:38.380 --> 00:18:41.230
How can you work with someone who's gone?

00:18:45.820 --> 00:18:50.830
I see!  Even if Honda isn't here, we can work together!

00:18:51.040 --> 00:18:52.770
Okay!  It's our final chance!

00:18:53.440 --> 00:18:56.710
I activate my Deck Master's ability!

00:18:58.130 --> 00:19:03.080
I discard two cards from my hand to activate Honda's set card!

00:19:03.300 --> 00:19:04.020
What?

00:19:06.650 --> 00:19:10.180
Honda, everything depends on the card you left us.

00:19:10.580 --> 00:19:12.320
Don't let me down.

00:19:12.570 --> 00:19:13.490
Come on!

00:19:13.850 --> 00:19:15.430
Honda's card...

00:19:16.900 --> 00:19:20.480
Rin.  Hyo.  Tou.  Sha.

00:19:20.480 --> 00:19:25.610
Kai.  Jin.  Retsu.  Zai.  Zen.

00:19:28.300 --> 00:19:29.840
Rare Metal Soul?

00:19:29.840 --> 00:19:32.850
All right!  I activate Rare Metal Soul!

00:19:32.850 --> 00:19:38.380
The Fusion Monster St. Joan gains 1000 attack points!

00:19:43.150 --> 00:19:44.360
What?

00:19:44.680 --> 00:19:46.400
Their attack points are equal.

00:19:46.400 --> 00:19:47.360
They're both gone?

00:19:47.360 --> 00:19:47.890
No.

00:19:47.890 --> 00:19:49.230
Shizuka!

00:19:49.230 --> 00:19:53.900
St. Joan carries on Honda's wishes.  Show him her power!

00:19:53.900 --> 00:19:54.770
Okay!

00:19:55.020 --> 00:19:58.700
St. Joan, attack Perfect Machine King!

00:20:13.480 --> 00:20:15.190
How dare you!

00:20:22.160 --> 00:20:25.060
I shouldn't have summoned my Deck Master!

00:20:25.500 --> 00:20:26.830
You did it, Shizuka!

00:20:26.830 --> 00:20:27.730
- They won!

00:20:26.830 --> 00:20:27.730
- Yeah!

00:20:27.940 --> 00:20:32.170
I lost the duel, but I acquired one body.

00:20:32.380 --> 00:20:33.140
What?

00:20:33.140 --> 00:20:34.290
A body?

00:20:34.800 --> 00:20:36.180
You mean Honda?

00:20:36.350 --> 00:20:38.820
I've achieved my goal.

00:20:40.470 --> 00:20:42.730
This will get interesting.

00:20:42.730 --> 00:20:43.900
See you soon!

00:20:57.380 --> 00:21:02.300
No...  Honda isn't coming back.

00:21:02.600 --> 00:21:03.720
Shizuka!

00:21:09.690 --> 00:21:10.740
Shizuka.

00:21:11.900 --> 00:21:16.640
Honda's gone because of me!

00:21:17.660 --> 00:21:19.020
Shizuka...

00:21:19.550 --> 00:21:22.690
Honda, I promise to save you.

00:21:22.900 --> 00:21:25.690
Damn!  The Big Five!

00:21:25.690 --> 00:21:27.450
Give Honda back!

00:21:44.680 --> 00:21:48.600
We defeated The Big Five, so why hasn't Honda returned?

00:21:48.600 --> 00:21:50.510
We split apart and search.

00:21:50.510 --> 00:21:53.250
Honda kidnaps Mokuba and flees!

00:21:53.250 --> 00:21:54.540
What are you doing?

00:21:54.540 --> 00:21:57.450
Have you really been possessed?

00:21:57.720 --> 00:22:01.870
Kaiba gives chase, but the last Big Five blocks his way.

00:22:01.870 --> 00:22:04.730
And what's with this monkey?

00:22:05.100 --> 00:22:09.350
Next time on Yu-Gi-Oh!:
Mokuba Kidnapped
Kaiba vs Jinzo

00:22:09.350 --> 00:22:10.900
Duel, standby!

00:22:14.620 --> 00:22:22.520
The sun never sets
It rises forever

00:22:22.520 --> 00:22:31.470
Don't let a dream end as a dream

00:22:31.800 --> 00:22:36.440
The straight rail and harsh route

00:22:36.440 --> 00:22:40.410
Whether to go or not 
all of yourself

00:22:40.840 --> 00:22:48.380
I'm tired of counting on my fingers inside this cage

00:22:48.380 --> 00:22:51.950
Respect! Boys  Show me how you act tough

00:22:51.950 --> 00:22:56.720
Draw a map, even if it's sloppy

00:22:56.720 --> 00:23:06.830
And walk it without stopping

00:23:06.830 --> 00:23:14.440
The sun never sets
If I can be like you

00:23:14.670 --> 00:23:23.410
Create freedom by exceeding common ideas

00:23:23.410 --> 00:23:31.390
I want to trust myself
Sometimes I'll lose my way but

00:23:31.390 --> 00:23:41.230
I hide it in my heart...
Secret Paradise
